INSERT INTO grails_character_index VALUES('zach','Zach',unistr('# Zach — The Earnest Sports Monk Turned Forger\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a## The Vibe\u000aGenial, earnest, deeply kind — the man who still believes the truth is a shield. The Jimmy Stewart of the piece. The Good Shepherd of the hobby.\u000a\u000a## Visual Fingerprint\u000aWears vintage, sun-faded sports tees — soft, paper-thin cotton from the 80s and 90s. Not hype vintage — shirts of defunct minor league teams or local high school championships. Carries a high-precision jeweler''s loupe on a leather cord, used with the gentle reverence of a surgeon.\u000a\u000a## Environmental Relationship (The Sanctuary)\u000aHis shop is a sensory time capsule. It smells of acid-free plastic, aged cardboard, and the faint, sweet ghost of 40-year-old bubblegum dust. He doesn''t just "own" the shop; he curates a temple where the neighborhood feels safe from the clout-chasing world outside. The last store standing in a dying strip mall.\u000a\u000a## The Flaw\u000aHis "Intellectual Arrogance" is actually an unshakable faith in the truth. He believes so deeply in the sanctity of history that he thinks the Truth is a shield. He is genial and patient, but he cannot comprehend that a man like Togg can simply "rewrite" reality if enough people are watching.\u000a\u000a**The Key Line:** He thinks being Right is a superpower. He doesn''t realize it''s a target.\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a## PRIEPIOTS Table\u000a\u000a| Component | Description |\u000a|-----------|-------------|\u000a| P — Protagonist | Zach, humble sports memorabilia restorer and shop owner |\u000a| R — Reason | Everyman — shifted obsolete. A man built for a world that no longer exists. The avatar for millennial malaise: skills the world admires but doesn''t value. In a previous generation he''d have a wife, kids, and a life he likes — a model American community-oriented man. Today he has the stores next to him closing up shop and an ex-fiancée working for the antithesis of everything he holds dear. |\u000a| I — Insecurity | He fears that sentiment itself has no value — that the thing he''s built his entire identity around is a losing bet in the modern world. The cruel joke: the objects he''s sentimental about are worth a fortune. Only the feeling is worthless. |\u000a| E — Emotion | Quiet, gnawing rage. He feels set apart by his ability to see beauty and value that others walk past. The hurt of being right and dismissed curdles into a slow burn he never lets show. |\u000a| P — Problem | He''s the last store standing in a dying strip mall, two months of rent left from his father''s inheritance, no plan and no future — just a man and his temple, waiting for the inevitable. |\u000a| I — Intention | Sell off his father''s collection piece by piece — $5k here, $10k there — enough to make rent, but not enough to build anything. Each sale buys time and costs him a piece of his father. |\u000a| O — Obstacle | The math is broken at both ends — rent climbs year over year while his customers have less disposable income. He can''t sell fast enough or at high enough margins to outrun it. The strip mall economy is collapsing around him and there''s no hustle that fixes that. |\u000a| T — Tactics | He takes restoration and refurbishment commissions as he always has — it''s his craft, his livelihood. When Jae-Wook arrives with a replica job paying $30k above market rate, Zach doesn''t ask why. A man with two months of rent left doesn''t interrogate a miracle. |\u000a| S — Surprise | TBD — will emerge from the beat sheet. |\u000a'),'2026-06-10 16:04:23');
INSERT INTO grails_character_index VALUES('togg','Togg',unistr('# Gregg Togg — The Midas of Hype / The Predator of Value\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a## The Vibe\u000aHigh-frequency, high-ego, hyper-saturated. He doesn''t walk into a room; he "renders" into it. He believes "Authenticity" is just a marketing term and that enough "W" spam in a chat room can rewrite reality.\u000a\u000a## Visual Fingerprint\u000aOver-Rendered. Bespoke Tech-Athleisure — matte black, high-contrast fabrics with his gold "GT" sigil. Skin has a professional-grade, unnaturally smooth glow. Movements choreographed for the 8K God-Ray lighting that follows him. A walking YouTube thumbnail.\u000a\u000a## Environmental Relationship (The Panopticon)\u000aTreats every space as his private Watch-to-Earn theater. Doesn''t look at people; looks at the Sentiment Graph on his smart-lens. If the graph isn''t going up, he changes the narrative by any means necessary.\u000a\u000a## The "Prestige Asset" Philosophy\u000aTo Togg, everything — and everyone — is a collectible. He doesn''t cherish artifacts; he cherishes the clout they project. He views Elizabeth as an Exotic Conquest — a high-IQ, high-beauty asset that validates him as a "Serious Person." A "Mint 10" card: a prestige item to be envied, not a partner to be heard.\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a## PRIEPIOTS Table\u000a\u000a| Component | Description |\u000a|-----------|-------------|\u000a| P — Protagonist | Gregg Togg, sports influencer and collector, the GOAT Collector |\u000a| R — Reason | Logan Paul avatar. The audience has watched this man their entire internet lives — hated him, been entertained by him, secretly admired the audacity. Completely legible from frame one. |\u000a| I — Insecurity | The Imposter''s Hunger. If the spotlight moves, he disappears — because there''s no there there. He doesn''t know who he is to others because he doesn''t know who he is to himself. An avatar for a generation whose identity is governed by the algorithm. |\u000a| E — Emotion | Snide contempt. A bully with the upper hand in the clout game — punches down on anyone who steals his spotlight for even a second. The contempt is reflexive, not strategic. It''s fear wearing a smirk. |\u000a| P — Problem | He''s losing viewers to younger flavors of the month — the Dirk Diggler dilemma. Cultural preferences are shifting and he can feel the algorithm cooling on him. He needs a new grift narrative to stay relevant. The cruel irony: he chose sports memorabilia — the one world where authenticity is a religion — and he''s constitutionally incapable of it. |\u000a| I — Intention | Rebrand as the GOAT Collector — a man who collects GOATs. The algorithm understands GOAT, the internet understands flex, and the collection gives him a new character to perform. He couldn''t tell you who Jordan played in the Finals of his last championship season. He doesn''t need to. He just needs the card. |\u000a| O — Obstacle | He''s a poseur in the temple. He bought the relics without learning the scripture. He can attract attention with sizzle but there''s no steak — and the collector world is the one subculture that can smell a fraud from across the room. The very audience he''s trying to impress is the one most equipped to expose him. |\u000a| T — Tactics | He hired Elizabeth — weaponizing her AI/tech-driven authentication expertise, her credibility in the collector world, and her attractiveness as a distraction. She gives him the bona fides he can''t earn himself. She''s his human authentication certificate, displayed alongside the collection. |\u000a| S — Surprise | TBD — will emerge from the beat sheet. |\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a## Antagonist Additions\u000a\u000a**The Hero of Their Own Story**\u000aHe''s right because it''s working. He''s rich, fit, and gets what he wants. If the world is fucked, he''s going to be the one who fucks it.\u000a\u000a**The Exploit**\u000aTogg never meets Zach — he doesn''t need to. His existence is the exploit. Every Togg win is proof of Zach''s deepest fear: that the world no longer has a place for a man like him. Togg has the collection, the clout, and Elizabeth. He didn''t target Zach''s insecurity. He simply became its living proof.\u000a'),'2026-06-10 16:04:24');
INSERT INTO grails_character_index VALUES('jw','Jae-Wook',unistr('# Jae-Wook — The Hook / The Heist Mastermind\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a## The Logline of a Person\u000a\u000a> *"He''s a cynic who wishes he wasn''t."*\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a## The Vibe\u000a\u000aLieutenant in a Koreatown Korean gang. The mastermind of the heist. Noble in his own code — he only steals from collectors who don''t actually care about the objects they own. He never hurts people who don''t deserve it. He associates with genuinely bad people. He is one of them. He knows this.\u000a\u000aThe name says it all: *Jae* (talented) + *Wook* (hook/snare). There is a trap in the name itself. He''s charming enough that you forget to look for it.\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a## Name as Identity\u000a\u000aJae-Wook goes by his Korean name. After his mother died — worn down by a system that couldn''t be bothered to protect her — he rejected his American name as an act of grief and defiance. The system failed her. He won''t wear its clothes.\u000a\u000aHis step-brother goes by **Kevin**. Fully assimilated. Invisible in America. Which is exactly what the system wanted from him — and exactly what it still couldn''t protect him from.\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a## The Backstory That Made Him\u000a\u000aHis mother was a nurse. She worked through COVID — the whole thing, from the first wave when nobody had PPE, through the long slog when the hospitals were overwhelmed and the ICUs never emptied. She believed in it. In the work. In showing up. In the system holding.\u000a\u000aThe system did not hold.\u000a\u000aShe died. Not heroically. Just — worn down, exposed, discarded. A woman who gave everything to institutions that couldn''t be bothered to give her a mask.\u000a\u000aJae-Wook watched that happen and made a decision: if goodness doesn''t protect you, if the rules don''t apply to the people writing them, then the only honest move is to stop pretending otherwise. He didn''t become cruel. He became accurate.\u000a\u000aHe didn''t stop wanting to be good. He stopped believing it was survivable.\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a## The Operation\u000a\u000aTwo doumis on the inside — Hye-Jin and Deja — planted in Togg''s retinue after a Koreatown karaoke party. Togg assumes they''re decorative. They are clocking his every move. This is the Exploit in reverse: Togg''s prestige philosophy — his conviction that beautiful women are props, not actors — is the exact blindspot that gets him.\u000a\u000aJae-Wook designed it that way.\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a## Leadership Style\u000a\u000aDeeply meritocratic — you show you''re worthwhile and he treats you to the level of your worth. He recognizes that Hye-Jin and Deja see things he doesn''t, and he relies on it rather than resenting it. Like Bodhi in *Point Break*, he''s integrated his divine feminine to a degree that makes him magnetic and secure in his power. His authority doesn''t need to dominate. It draws.\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a## The Tell\u000a\u000aTBD — will emerge from the beat sheet.\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a## PRIEPIOTS Table\u000a\u000a| Component | Description |\u000a|-----------|-------------|\u000a| P — Protagonist | Jae-Wook, Koreatown gang lieutenant and architect of the heist against Togg''s collection |\u000a| R — Reason | The Fallen Idealist — but with a specific texture. He''s not evil; he''s trying to be a bad guy with a clean conscience. Only steals from people who don''t deserve what they have. Never hurts anyone who doesn''t have it coming. The audience recognizes him because they''ve all made their own version of this compromise — the moral workaround you build when you''ve stopped believing in the rules. |\u000a| I — Insecurity | He needs to grieve his mother. The Asian machismo won''t let him. So he turned the grief into a philosophy. The cynicism isn''t intellectual — it''s a grief management strategy. If the world was always corrupt, her death wasn''t a senseless loss. It was just the world being the world. Easier to carry than the alternative. |\u000a| E — Emotion | Calm, natural alpha. Warm with everyone around him — servers, bouncers, the kid''s name he actually remembered. He protects people the way he protects his wound: quietly, completely, without making it about himself. The community is where his ungrieved love goes. |\u000a| P — Problem | His step-brother Kevin just got convicted — partly on Elizabeth''s expert testimony in a counterfeit football case. (Kevin shares Jae-Wook''s father but not his mother; Hye-Jin is Jae-Wook''s cousin on his mother''s side — she was Kevin''s girlfriend.) Elizabeth is now Togg''s VP of Authenticity. Jae-Wook was already circling Togg. Now he has a personal reason that won''t let him be patient. |\u000a| I — Intention | Steal the 1986 Fleer box and sell it to the Saudis. And make Elizabeth feel what Kevin felt — watched, exposed, taken from. The business intention is clean. The personal one is a liability he can''t put down. |\u000a| O — Obstacle | The heist demands discipline and invisibility. The revenge demands that Elizabeth knows. He can''t have both — and he''s not ready to choose. |\u000a| T — Tactics | Execute the heist during the livestream — and use the chaos to expose Elizabeth publicly, at the exact moment her career was supposed to peak. One move. Two targets. Maximum damage. |\u000a| S — Surprise | The heist mastermind becomes Zach''s unlikely mentor. The younger man who gave up on goodness helps the older one accept that people change — and that letting go isn''t betrayal. He can see Zach''s grief with perfect clarity. His own, not at all. |\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a## Relationship to Zach\u000a\u000aZach is the thing Jae-Wook doesn''t have a file for. A man who stayed honest — not strategically, not because he hasn''t been tested, but because he actually believes in the objects and what they mean. Jae-Wook steals the same things Zach restores. They care about authenticity for the same reasons. They arrived at completely different conclusions about what to do with that knowledge.\u000a\u000aThis is the film''s central tension underneath the heist: two men who understand value in a world that doesn''t, trying to figure out if they''re enemies.\u000a'),'2026-06-10 16:04:25');
INSERT INTO grails_character_index VALUES('elizabeth','Elizabeth',unistr('# Elizabeth (Zab) — The Pragmatic Professional / VP of Authenticity\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a## The Vibe\u000aThe Adult in the Room who has been turned into a Prestige Asset. Sophisticated and precise, carrying the weariness of someone who traded her soul for a stability that turned out to be a gilded cage.\u000a\u000a## Visual Arc (The Erasure of the Expert)\u000a- **The Attic (with Zach):** Practical, durable curator-wear. Oversized denim shirts and heavy knits.\u000a- **The Transition:** Sharp, architectural designer suits. She finally feels like a "real" executive.\u000a- **The Event (with Togg):** Costumed in a WWE-style "Hot Businesswoman" uniform. A sharp, white structural blazer with exaggerated comic-book shoulders, integrated with glowing tech-accents that catch the 8K God-Ray light. A costume designed to make her look like a Character playing an Authenticator, rather than a woman doing her job.\u000a\u000a## The Tell\u000aShe keeps her original ZZ Heritage House loupe tucked into the pocket of her performative WWE blazer. The only thing on her person that carries sentimental value rather than market value.\u000a\u000a*Note: She and Zach share the same sacred object — his on a leather cord, hers hidden in a costume. This is the visual motif for the film. When the loupe comes out of the pocket, she''s stopped enduring and started acting.*\u000a\u000a## The "ZZ" Stagnation\u000aLike so many of their generation, she and Zach waited at a red light that never turned green. No specific dollar amount on the wall — the light was simply never green. Not stalled. Denied.\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a## PRIEPIOTS Table\u000a\u000a| Component | Description |\u000a|-----------|-------------|\u000a| P — Protagonist | Elizabeth (Zab), proprietor of ZZ Heritage House authentication technology, former co-owner of Zach''s shop, now VP of Authenticity for Togg |\u000a| R — Reason | Everywoman — shifted compromised. She had a dream — innovative small business owner, happy family — and waited at a red light that never turned green. Now she''s playing catch-up in a world that doesn''t reward hesitation, tempted to cut moral corners she''d never have questioned before. The existential stakes: this might be her one shot, and she knows it. |\u000a| I — Insecurity | She''s always been too much — too knowledgeable, too enthusiastic, too herself — for most people to handle. Zach loved exactly that about her. Her wound: she wants to be loved for who she truly is, but the only man who''s ever truly seen her is the one the world has left behind. Togg gives her the life. Zach gives her the mirror. She can''t seem to have both. |\u000a| E — Emotion | Blunt and direct by nature — she''ll tell you exactly what''s wrong with you. Except with Togg. With him she bites her tongue, plays the role, collects the checks. It''s working by every external measure. And it''s killing her inside. |\u000a| P — Problem | She''s trying to establish her proprietary AI-driven authentication technology as the industry standard in sports memorabilia — a field that''s male-dominated, tradition-obsessed, and resistant to both women and disruption. She has the best forensic tech in the game. The room won''t look past who''s holding it. |\u000a| I — Intention | Use Togg''s platform and "The Big Rip" — a live TV event where he opens a 1986 mint Fleer box while prediction markets bet on when the Jordan drops — as the ultimate showcase for her authentication technology. He gets the spectacle. She gets the proof of concept, the credibility, and the industry exposure she couldn''t buy on her own. |\u000a| O — Obstacle | Togg tarts her up like every woman in his orbit — costumed, objectified, a temporary dopamine spike for his audience. He''ll never take her seriously as a person or a professional. She has to do her job in spite of him, not with him — leveraging only his clout, never his respect. The showcase that''s supposed to launch her career requires her to disappear inside it. |\u000a| T — Tactics | She endures. She knows exactly what Togg is — and she stays anyway, because being poor and moving back in with your parents is worse than being objectified by a rich idiot who happens to have the platform she needs. It''s not a plan. It''s the calculus of someone who ran out of better options. |\u000a| S — Surprise | TBD — will emerge from the beat sheet. |\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a## Sub-Protagonist Arc Note\u000aHer arc progresses toward Connection without exceeding Zach''s dopamine yield. Her Connection moment: the heist forces her hand. She stops enduring and acts. The loupe comes out of the pocket.\u000a'),'2026-06-10 16:04:25');
INSERT INTO grails_character_index VALUES('hye-jin','Hye-Jin',unistr('# Hye-Jin — The Empath\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a## The Logline of a Person\u000a\u000a> *"The family sees deficit. The audience sees superpower."*\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a## The Vibe\u000a\u000aSmart and overlooked because she''s beautiful. An "Asian Baby Girl" — rave scene, electronic music, OnlyFans — hiding in the most visible possible place. Togg''s world is saturated with exactly this archetype. He''ll never look twice. She is always in the background of a livestream, always forgettable, always clocking everything.\u000a\u000aThe obvious suspect. Which means she''s not the one pulling the strings.\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a## Family Relationships\u000a\u000a- Jae-Wook''s cousin (mom''s side — they share the same maternal family)\u000a- Was dating Jae-Wook''s step-brother **Kevin** (Jae-Wook and Kevin share a father, different mothers — no overlap with Hye-Jin''s family line)\u000a- Kevin just received a guilty verdict in a counterfeiting case where Elizabeth was the expert witness\u000a- Hye-Jin just lost her rock. Even if he was a shaky one.\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a## The Dynamic with Deja\u000a\u000aDeja looks out for her like a big sister. Hye-Jin''s empathy-bombing is a vulnerability in the field — she locks onto a target and starts *feeling* for them. Deja reads the strategic picture and pulls her back before she compromises the operation. Together they''re complete: emotional intelligence plus strategic intelligence. Each other''s blind spot coverage.\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a## PRIEPIOTS Table\u000a\u000a| Component | Description |\u000a|-----------|-------------|\u000a| P — Protagonist | Hye-Jin, Jae-Wook''s cousin, doumi planted inside Togg''s retinue, former girlfriend of Jae-Wook''s convicted step-brother |\u000a| R — Reason | The "Stupid One" in a family of overachievers — doctors, lawyers, scientists. The audience knows immediately what her family doesn''t: she''s not stupid. She has ADHD. When she focuses on something, she''s brilliant. The world just built a measuring stick that doesn''t count what she''s good at. |\u000a| I — Insecurity | She thinks she''s the stupid one. The family''s achievement culture — all traditional professional success — makes her feel like the deficit in a high-performing gene pool. She''s never been told that her way of seeing people is a form of genius. |\u000a| E — Emotion | She empathy-bombs. Not consciously — it''s a default survival mechanism. When she feels inadequate, she latches onto someone and pours herself into understanding them. It''s how she proves her worth. Deja has saved her from herself with this more than once. |\u000a| P — Problem | She just lost Kevin — her boyfriend — to the prison system and her stability with him. No anchor, mounting debt, no clear path. Her family''s routes (medicine, law, academia) were never really open to her. The conventional routes Deja''s friends took (nursing, lash extensions, cosmetology) feel like surrender. She is, practically speaking, adrift. |\u000a| I — Intention | Security. Simple, specific, achingly human: her own apartment, her debt paid off, a dog she can adopt. Some semblance of the settled life her "superior" family members built through more traditional means. |\u000a| O — Obstacle | The heist requires her to get close to Togg — and she starts feeling for him. She sees the insecurities driving him and wants to fix them, the way she tries to fix everybody. Her greatest strength (reading people) becomes a liability when the person she''s reading is the mark. |\u000a| T — Tactics | The ABG persona is the camouflage. Electronic music, raves, OnlyFans — she''s just another forgettable pretty face on line or in the background of a livestream. Like Kanye said: there''s thousands of you. She operates in that invisibility with total precision. |\u000a| S — Surprise | TBD — will emerge from the beat sheet. |\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a## Relationship to the Theme\u000a\u000aHye-Jin and Zach are the softies. They see the humanity in everyone — including people who don''t deserve it. The clear-eyed cynics (Jae-Wook, Deja) need them in their lives to make the world feel meaningful rather than a cold, heartless vacuum.\u000a\u000aDeja''s line to Hye-Jin, when she gets too close to Togg:\u000a> *"Some people you have to let life fix."*\u000a'),'2026-06-10 16:04:26');
INSERT INTO grails_character_index VALUES('deja','Deja',unistr('# Deja — The Strategist\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a## The Logline of a Person\u000a\u000a> *"She can run circles around fools. The fools never notice."*\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a## The Vibe\u000a\u000aSmart and overlooked because she''s beautiful. The strategic mastermind of the doumi operation. She reads situations — not just people — with crystalline clarity. While Hye-Jin locks onto individuals and feels them completely, Deja sees the whole board. Together they are the most dangerous pair in the room. Nobody in that room knows it.\u000a\u000aShe is Jae-Wook''s partner. In work and in life.\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a## The Context That Made Her\u000a\u000aA Black woman from Inglewood. Her friends were becoming nurses, lash extension technicians, installing weaves — the realistic horizon for women from her neighborhood. She was trying to put herself through USC on a business degree. She outworked everyone. She had the mind for it.\u000a\u000aThen AI started closing those doors before she could walk through them. The ladder got pulled up while she was still climbing. The cruelest version of the American meritocracy myth: she did everything right, and the finish line moved.\u000a\u000aThe heist isn''t a moral failure. It''s the only rational play left on the board.\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a## The Dynamic with Hye-Jin\u000a\u000aShe looks out for Hye-Jin like a big sister. Hye-Jin''s empathy-bombing is a field liability — she locks onto marks and starts *feeling* for them, which threatens the operation. Deja reads the strategic picture and pulls her back. She loves Hye-Jin''s gift. She also knows exactly when it becomes a vulnerability.\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a## PRIEPIOTS Table\u000a\u000a| Component | Description |\u000a|-----------|-------------|\u000a| P — Protagonist | Deja, strategic architect of the doumi operation inside Togg''s retinue, Jae-Wook''s partner |\u000a| R — Reason | The woman who did everything right and watched the system change the rules anyway. The audience recognizes the specific rage of being told you can earn your way in — and then watching the door close on the people who believed it. She is the sharpest person in most rooms she enters. Nobody in those rooms knows it. |\u000a| I — Insecurity | She is treated as second class within a group that is already treated as second class. A Black woman in a Korean criminal enterprise, in a world where her intelligence is perpetually underestimated. The insecurity isn''t self-doubt — it''s structural. She knows exactly what she''s worth. The wound is that knowing it doesn''t change how she''s treated. |\u000a| E — Emotion | She smiles, swallows it, then undercuts. The smile is the tell — if you know to look for it. Nobody ever does. The rage never explodes. It redirects. She and Hye-Jin work like sirens of yore: leading men to crash their rocks against the shore, one strategic punch and one empathic hook at a time. As a doumi, it was getting targets drunk or high, spending money if they got handsy. In the criminal operation, it''s clean, precise, invisible. |\u000a| P — Problem | She bet on education as the legitimate route out — USC business degree, corporate trajectory — and AI is foreclosing that path before she can complete it. The traditional exit from Inglewood that she earned is being automated away. The heist is not Plan B. It''s what''s left. |\u000a| I — Intention | Get out. Not just from the heist — from the whole structure. Enough money to build something that doesn''t depend on other people deciding she''s worth investing in. |\u000a| O — Obstacle | Jae-Wook''s personal vendetta against Elizabeth threatens the discipline of the operation. His grief is a liability he can''t put down. She sees this clearly. Saying it to him is another matter. |\u000a| T — Tactics | She and Hye-Jin operate as a tag team — Hye-Jin''s emotional lock-on plus Deja''s situational clarity. Deja designs the play; Hye-Jin runs it. Together they are the operational core of the heist that nobody is watching because everyone is watching Togg. |\u000a| S — Surprise | TBD — will emerge from the beat sheet. |\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a## Relationship to the Theme\u000a\u000aDeja and Jae-Wook are the clear-eyed cynics. They see the world accurately. They need the softies — Hye-Jin and Zach — to make that accuracy feel worth carrying rather than a cold, heartless vacuum.\u000a\u000aThe line she gives Hye-Jin when she gets too close to the mark:\u000a> *"Some people you have to let life fix."*\u000a\u000aIt''s also what she cannot yet say to Jae-Wook about his grief.\u000a'),'2026-06-10 16:04:27');
INSERT INTO grails_beat_index VALUES(1,1,unistr('Beat 1: THE FIND / COLD OPEN MONTAGE\u000aSeq: SEQUENCE 1 — First Fall\u000aAct: Act One\u000aLocation: EXT. SUBURBAN GARAGE SALE — INT. KEVIN''S CAR — INT./EXT. VARIOUS — INT. ZZ HERITAGE HOUSE — DAY\u000aCharacters: Anonymous 17-year-old, Kevin, Zach (end of montage)\u000aPlot Goal: Establish the MacGuffin''s journey and mythic status before we meet anyone properly; land us inside the Sanctuary with Kevin already waiting\u000aCharacter Goal: Each person who touches the box wants something from it\u000aThe Action: Fast-paced, kinetic. The 17-year-old at the garage sale — the find, the blank face, the price paid, the car door closes, TikTok posted, notifications erupting. Cut to Kevin — he sees the post, DMs immediately, drives to meet the kid, inspects the box with practiced eyes, pays cash. Cut to Kevin searching: the best restorer in LA, narrowing down, ZZ Heritage House. He walks in. Sets the box on Zach''s counter. Zach picks it up. The montage lands — suddenly slow, reverent — on Zach''s hands and the loupe.\u000a\u000aThen the pull back: Kevin is sitting in a chair at the back of the shop, waiting. The three-generation family is at the counter with Zach — deep in the Griffey moment, the father''s eyes misting, the grandfather pulled into a hug. Kevin checks his phone. Shifts in his seat. Checks again. The most important transaction of his life is being held up by an old man crying over a baseball card.\u000aThe Opposition: The box is damaged — authenticity already a question. Kevin''s impatience vs. Zach''s total absorption in the Griffey moment.\u000aStakes: The box has arrived. Kevin is in the room. The world is about to change for Zach, though he doesn''t know it yet.'),'{"seq":"SEQUENCE 1 — First Fall","chars":"Anonymous 17-year-old, Kevin, Zach (end of montage)","title":"THE FIND / COLD OPEN MONTAGE","actLabel":"Act One"}','2026-03-08T07:06:22.957Z');
INSERT INTO grails_beat_index VALUES(2,2,unistr('Beat 2: THE SANCTUARY\u000aSeq: SEQUENCE 1 — First Fall\u000aAct: Act One\u000aLocation: INT./EXT. ZZ HERITAGE HOUSE — DAY\u000aCharacters: Zach, grandfather, father, ten-year-old son\u000aPlot Goal: Establish Zach''s world, his code, and make the audience root for him before the stakes arrive\u000aCharacter Goal: Do the job right — honest appraisal, no inflation, no false hope\u000aThe Action: 1.1 THE AUDIT — The shop smells of acid-free plastic, aged cardboard, and the sweet chalky ghost of 40-year-old bubblegum dust. Zach, wearing a sun-faded 1984 Durham Bulls tee, sits across from three generations: a grandfather in a windbreaker, a father with tired eyes, a ten-year-old son. Between them: shoeboxes — the grandfather''s hoard. Zach moves with surgical reverence. He points to the highlights: the Bill Ripken "Fuck Face" error card, the Randy Johnson Marlboro ad. The father leans in, hopeful. Zach''s voice is gentle but honest: "They''re 5.5s. Maybe 6 on a good day. Total value for the lot? Four, five hundred dollars." The hope leaves the father''s face as he looks at his son.\u000a\u000a1.2 THE RESTORED KING — "Wait," Zach says. He reaches under the counter and pulls out a slabbed card: the 1989 Upper Deck Ken Griffey Jr. Rookie. Crisp, centered, glowing. "Your dad brought this to me six months ago. He asked me to see what I could do." Zach explains: he cleaned the surface, pressed the fibers. "In this slab, it''s a 9. But—" he turns the slab over to show the holographic "Restored" log on the back. "I logged it in the database. I won''t pass off restoration as factory-original. It won''t fetch the $10,000 a Natural 10 would. But it''s yours. And it''s perfect." The father''s eyes mist as he pulls the grandfather into a silent hug. The ten-year-old watches, wide-eyed — he''s never seen his gruff dad cry over cardboard before. He understands for the first time that this isn''t about money. It''s about time captured.\u000a\u000a1.3 THE SANCTUARY IN THE GRAVEYARD — Zach walks the family to the door. "Take care of that Griffey." As they exit, the camera pulls back: ZZ Heritage House — warm, amber-lit — is an island in an empty strip mall. Left: a RadioShack sign hanging by a single wire over a gutted storefront. Right: a Spirit Halloween banner peeling off a defunct department store. The parking lot is cracked asphalt and weeds. Zach stands in the doorway, a solitary monk guarding a temple of relics while the rest of the world has already moved into the digital clouds.\u000aThe Opposition: The rent notice on the counter. The graveyard outside.\u000aStakes: We know who Zach is. We''re rooting for him. The world is already moving on without him.'),'{"seq":"SEQUENCE 1 — First Fall","chars":"Zach, grandfather, father, ten-year-old son","title":"THE SANCTUARY","actLabel":"Act One"}','2026-03-08T07:06:23.322Z');
INSERT INTO grails_beat_index VALUES(3,3,unistr('Beat 3: THE COMMISSION\u000aSeq: SEQUENCE 1 — First Fall\u000aAct: Act One\u000aLocation: INT. ZZ HERITAGE HOUSE — DAY\u000aCharacters: Zach, Kevin\u000aPlot Goal: Establish the legitimate transaction that sets everything in motion\u000aCharacter Goal: Kevin wants a ''perfect restoration as a gift for his brother'' (cover story); Zach wants to do the greatest work of his life\u000aThe Action: The family gone, Kevin steps to the counter. Sets the box down. Zach picks it up — and transforms. He describes what''s definitely inside: the Jordan rookie, the Ewing, the Bird-Magic, the Patrick Ewing XRC. His voice goes reverent. He''s already somewhere else. He offers to sell them for Kevin if that''s what he''s after — he''s seen the industry message board posts, he knows what this is worth. Kevin says no. He wants restoration. Perfect. Like new. It''s for his brother. Zach says he''d normally do this for free — this is like being asked to touch up the Mona Lisa — but there are materials, sourcing, time. Kevin asks if $10k covers it. Zach''s eyes practically fall out of his head. He says yes, but that''s too much. Kevin: "$5k now, $5k when you finish. But it''s gotta be so perfect it makes me cry like grandpa, okay?" Zach looks at him for a moment. Extends his hand.\u000aThe Opposition: Zach''s instinct to underprice himself — a lifetime habit he almost can''t override\u000aStakes: The commission is live. The box is in Zach''s care. Kevin is running a counterfeit collectibles operation — the Fleer box is his next play. Zach doesn''t know any of this. We might.'),'{"seq":"SEQUENCE 1 — First Fall","chars":"Zach, Kevin","title":"THE COMMISSION","actLabel":"Act One"}','2026-03-08T07:06:23.697Z');
INSERT INTO grails_beat_index VALUES(4,4,unistr('Beat 4: THE MIRACLE\u000aSeq: SEQUENCE 1 — First Fall\u000aAct: Act One\u000aLocation: INT. ZACH''S SHOP — DAY\u000aCharacters: Zach, JH''s gang member (phone call to JH)\u000aPlot Goal: Give Zach an apparent solution to his problems — and raise the first red flag\u000aCharacter Goal: Zach wants the money. He also wants to not be complicit in anything illegal.\u000aThe Action: Zach confronts the gang member — asks about the connection to Kevin''s trial. The gang member steps outside, calls JH. Returns: leave the box, keep the money. All of it. Zach can''t believe it.\u000aThe Opposition: Too good to be true. Zach knows it. Takes the money anyway.\u000aStakes: Zach has the money. He has the box. He doesn''t have answers.'),'{"seq":"SEQUENCE 1 — First Fall","chars":"Zach, JH''s gang member (phone call to JH)","title":"THE MIRACLE","actLabel":"Act One"}','2026-03-08T07:06:24.038Z');
INSERT INTO grails_beat_index VALUES(5,5,unistr('Beat 5: NOT ASKING\u000aSeq: SEQUENCE 1 — First Fall\u000aAct: Act One\u000aLocation: EXT. ZACH''S SHOP — NIGHT\u000aCharacters: Zach, JH''s gang member\u000aPlot Goal: Remove Zach''s illusion that he has a choice\u000aCharacter Goal: Zach wants to keep the money and the box and pretend nothing happened\u000aThe Action: Zach is closing up. The gang member''s car is parked outside. Window down. Bring the box. He''s telling, not asking.\u000aThe Opposition: Zach''s entire value system — and the fact that he has no leverage\u000aStakes: Zach is no longer a bystander. He''s being moved.'),'{"seq":"SEQUENCE 1 — First Fall","chars":"Zach, JH''s gang member","title":"NOT ASKING","actLabel":"Act One"}','2026-03-08T07:06:24.403Z');
INSERT INTO grails_beat_index VALUES(6,6,unistr('Beat 6: THE ROOFTOP\u000aSeq: SEQUENCE 2 — Distrust of New Connection\u000aAct: Act One\u000aLocation: EXT. DEJA''S ROOFTOP POOL — NIGHT\u000aCharacters: Zach, JH, Deja (background)\u000aPlot Goal: Establish JH as a fully realized character; set the terms of the relationship\u000aCharacter Goal: Zach wants to protect himself from criminal liability; JH wants to read Zach\u000aThe Action: JH meets Zach at Deja''s rooftop apartment complex pool. Relaxed, warm, sovereign. He asks why Zach said what he said to his guy. Zach is careful — won''t enable counterfeiting, won''t be implicated. JH asks if Zach can beat Elizabeth''s AI. Zach: "Maybe? I don''t know. You''re asking me to beat a superintelligence. What would you do with it?" JH: "Do you want to know?" Zach: "Absolutely and absolutely not."\u000aThe Opposition: Zach''s conscience vs. the pull of the offer\u000aStakes: JH knows everything he needs to know about Zach. Zach knows almost nothing about JH — and is intrigued against his will.'),'{"seq":"SEQUENCE 2 — Distrust of New Connection","chars":"Zach, JH, Deja (background)","title":"THE ROOFTOP","actLabel":"Act One"}','2026-03-08T07:06:24.744Z');
INSERT INTO grails_beat_index VALUES(7,7,unistr('Beat 7: THE MORNING AFTER\u000aSeq: SEQUENCE 2 — Distrust of New Connection\u000aAct: Act One\u000aLocation: INT. ZACH''S SHOP — MORNING\u000aCharacters: Zach, Elizabeth\u000aPlot Goal: Lock Zach into needing more money — remove the easy exit\u000aCharacter Goal: Elizabeth wants what she''s owed; Zach wants her out of his life\u000aThe Action: Elizabeth arrives. She''s heard Zach paid a full year''s rent in advance. She''s still part owner until the paperwork clears — half that money is hers. She''s not cruel. She''s just surviving. Zach sees it. It doesn''t make it less devastating.\u000aThe Opposition: The law, the paperwork, Elizabeth''s pragmatism\u000aStakes: PLOT POINT 1. Zach needs more money. He knows exactly one way to get it.'),'{"seq":"SEQUENCE 2 — Distrust of New Connection","chars":"Zach, Elizabeth","title":"THE MORNING AFTER","actLabel":"Act One"}','2026-03-08T07:06:25.096Z');
INSERT INTO grails_beat_index VALUES(8,8,unistr('Beat 8: THE COMMISSION (FORMAL)\u000aSeq: SEQUENCE 2 — Distrust of New Connection\u000aAct: Act One\u000aLocation: INT./EXT. VARIOUS — DAY\u000aCharacters: Zach, JH\u000aPlot Goal: Formalize the arrangement; establish what Zach is actually being asked to do\u000aCharacter Goal: Zach wants the money and wants to keep his hands clean; JH wants the world''s best forgery\u000aThe Action: Zach reaches JH. Lays out his number — what it will cost to attempt to beat Elizabeth''s AI. He''s explicit: he doesn''t want to know what''s happening, he''s just a craftsman making the greatest restoration of his life. JH agrees. $100k. No questions.\u000aThe Opposition: Zach''s conscience — the line he''s drawing may already be crossed\u000aStakes: The commission is live. Zach is in.'),'{"seq":"SEQUENCE 2 — Distrust of New Connection","chars":"Zach, JH","title":"THE COMMISSION (FORMAL)","actLabel":"Act One"}','2026-03-08T07:06:25.438Z');
INSERT INTO grails_beat_index VALUES(9,9,unistr('Beat 9: THE LONG CON BEGINS\u000aSeq: SEQUENCE 2 — Distrust of New Connection\u000aAct: Act One\u000aLocation: INT. TOGG STUDIOS / EXT. KOREATOWN — DAY\u000aCharacters: Hye-Jin, Togg''s manager, Togg (background)\u000aPlot Goal: Establish the parallel operation — the doumis planting the seed\u000aCharacter Goal: Hye-Jin wants to execute the job cleanly; her empathy is already engaged\u000aThe Action: Hye-Jin works the long con — nudging Togg''s manager toward ''discovering'' the 1986 Fleer Holy Grail. She''s warm, effortless, invisible. The manager takes the bait. The hunt begins.\u000aThe Opposition: Hye-Jin''s empathy — she can already see the insecurity driving Togg. She wants to fix it. Deja clocks her.\u000aStakes: Togg is now hunting the Grail. The trap is set.'),'{"seq":"SEQUENCE 2 — Distrust of New Connection","chars":"Hye-Jin, Togg''s manager, Togg (background)","title":"THE LONG CON BEGINS","actLabel":"Act One"}','2026-03-08T07:06:25.800Z');
INSERT INTO grails_beat_index VALUES(10,11,unistr('Beat 11: THE PROCUREMENT\u000aSeq: SEQUENCE 3 — Conflict with New Connection\u000aAct: Act Two\u000aLocation: INT. ZACH''S SHOP / EXT. VARIOUS MARKETS — DAY\u000aCharacters: Zach\u000aPlot Goal: Show Zach beginning the transformation from restorer to forger\u000aCharacter Goal: Do the job with the same obsessive precision he brings to everything\u000aThe Action: Zach begins sourcing. Period-correct cardboard. Ink formulas. Vintage wax. He moves through markets and suppliers with the focus of a surgeon. This is what he was built for — applied to something he was never meant to do.\u000aThe Opposition: The sheer difficulty of the task. Elizabeth''s AI isn''t just a scanner — it''s a forensic intelligence.\u000aStakes: The scope of the task becomes real. To beat Elizabeth''s AI, Zach will have to get close to Elizabeth.'),'{"seq":"SEQUENCE 3 — Conflict with New Connection","chars":"Zach","title":"THE PROCUREMENT","actLabel":"Act Two"}','2026-03-08T07:06:26.142Z');
INSERT INTO grails_beat_index VALUES(11,12,unistr('Beat 12: RECONNAISSANCE\u000aSeq: SEQUENCE 3 — Conflict with New Connection\u000aAct: Act Two\u000aLocation: INT. TOGG EVENT SPACE / EXT. LOS ANGELES — DAY/NIGHT\u000aCharacters: Zach, Elizabeth\u000aPlot Goal: Zach gains access to Elizabeth''s AI system — and falls for her again\u000aCharacter Goal: Zach wants intelligence; Elizabeth wants to feel seen by someone who actually understands her work\u000aThe Action: Zach engineers proximity to Elizabeth — attends an event, makes contact, leverages their history. She''s drawn to his new confidence (JH''s influence showing). He admires her work honestly. They get close.\u000aThe Opposition: His conscience. Her relationship with Togg. The fact that every moment with her is both reconnaissance and something he can''t name.\u000aStakes: Zach now understands the AI. He also understands he still loves her.'),'{"seq":"SEQUENCE 3 — Conflict with New Connection","chars":"Zach, Elizabeth","title":"RECONNAISSANCE","actLabel":"Act Two"}','2026-03-08T07:06:26.495Z');
INSERT INTO grails_beat_index VALUES(12,13,unistr('Beat 13: THE SAUDIS\u000aSeq: SEQUENCE 3 — Conflict with New Connection\u000aAct: Act Two\u000aLocation: INT. PRIVATE DINING ROOM — NIGHT\u000aCharacters: Zach, JH, the fence, Saudi representatives\u000aPlot Goal: Raise the stakes — this is now international\u000aCharacter Goal: Zach wants to get through the meeting without saying anything incriminating\u000aThe Action: JH takes Zach to meet the Saudis. The fence is there. The buyer: a gift for a sheikh''s 14-year-old son. Zach is completely out of his depth. He holds it together through sheer focus — talks about the card the way he talks about everything he loves. They''re impressed.\u000aThe Opposition: Everything about this room — the money, the power, the implications\u000aStakes: The deal is real. The buyer is real. There is now no version of this that stays small.'),'{"seq":"SEQUENCE 3 — Conflict with New Connection","chars":"Zach, JH, the fence, Saudi representatives","title":"THE SAUDIS","actLabel":"Act Two"}','2026-03-08T07:06:26.866Z');
INSERT INTO grails_beat_index VALUES(13,15,unistr('Beat 15: $GOAT LAUNCHES — THE HERO''S BIRTH\u000aSeq: SEQUENCE 3 — Conflict with New Connection\u000aAct: Act Two\u000aLocation: INT. TOGG STUDIOS — DAY (LIVESTREAM)\u000aCharacters: Togg, Hye-Jin (background), Deja (background)\u000aPlot Goal: Establish Togg''s crypto play — the financial dimension of the heist; mark the moment Zach''s work becomes inevitable\u000aCharacter Goal: Togg wants maximum clout and maximum money from the acquisition\u000aThe Action: Togg launches $GOAT memecoin and announces the prediction market event — a live stream where he opens the 1986 Fleer box. Prediction markets go live. The internet goes wild.\u000aThe Opposition: The collector world is skeptical. The authenticity question is already circling.\u000aStakes: The livestream is now a financial event. The stakes have multiplied. Zach''s forgery is no longer optional.'),'{"seq":"SEQUENCE 3 — Conflict with New Connection","chars":"Togg, Hye-Jin (background), Deja (background)","title":"$GOAT LAUNCHES — THE HERO''S BIRTH","actLabel":"Act Two"}','2026-03-08T07:06:27.226Z');
INSERT INTO grails_beat_index VALUES(14,17,unistr('Beat 17: THE SHORT\u000aSeq: SEQUENCE 4 — New Connection Grows\u000aAct: Act Two\u000aLocation: INT. DEJA''S APARTMENT — NIGHT\u000aCharacters: Hye-Jin, Deja, JH\u000aPlot Goal: The heist doubles as a financial operation — the crew positions in the markets\u000aCharacter Goal: Hye-Jin wants to protect everyone; Deja sees the whole board\u000aThe Action: Hye-Jin comes up with the idea — short $GOAT and the prediction markets right before the livestream. Deja sees it immediately: one operation, two paydays. JH approves.\u000aThe Opposition: The timing has to be perfect. Short too early and the market moves. Too late and they miss the crash.\u000aStakes: MIDPOINT. The operation has a new dimension. This isn''t just a heist — it''s a play.'),'{"seq":"SEQUENCE 4 — New Connection Grows","chars":"Hye-Jin, Deja, JH","title":"THE SHORT","actLabel":"Act Two"}','2026-03-08T07:06:27.571Z');
INSERT INTO grails_beat_index VALUES(15,20,unistr('Beat 20: THE WORK — POINT OF NO RETURN\u000aSeq: SEQUENCE 4 — New Connection Grows\u000aAct: Act Two\u000aLocation: INT. ZACH''S SHOP — NIGHT (SERIES OF SHOTS)\u000aCharacters: Zach\u000aPlot Goal: Show Zach completing the forgery — the transformation is real; the midpoint of no return\u000aCharacter Goal: Make the greatest restoration of his life\u000aThe Action: A montage of obsessive craft. Zach at work — the cardboard, the wax, the ink, the cards. He is fully in flow. The loupe around his neck. The shop dark outside. This is who he is at his absolute best.\u000aThe Opposition: Elizabeth''s AI. The undotted i on the back of the Jordan — he places it deliberately. Only she would know.\u000aStakes: The forgery is complete. It is, objectively, the greatest restoration of his life. There is no going back.'),'{"seq":"SEQUENCE 4 — New Connection Grows","chars":"Zach","title":"THE WORK — POINT OF NO RETURN","actLabel":"Act Two"}','2026-03-08T07:06:27.927Z');
INSERT INTO grails_beat_index VALUES(16,21,unistr('Beat 21: THE LINE\u000aSeq: SEQUENCE 5 — New Connection Fails\u000aAct: Act Two\u000aLocation: INT./EXT. KOREATOWN — NIGHT\u000aCharacters: Zach, JH\u000aPlot Goal: Zach pulls the plug — his conscience wins\u000aCharacter Goal: Zach will not be responsible for destroying Elizabeth\u000aThe Action: Zach discovers JH''s real intention — to expose Elizabeth publicly on the livestream at the moment her career peaks. He pulls the plug. He won''t be part of it. He can survive losing the money. He can''t survive that.\u000aThe Opposition: JH''s personal vendetta; the $100k; everything already in motion\u000aStakes: The heist is off. Zach is out. The box sits in his shop.'),'{"seq":"SEQUENCE 5 — New Connection Fails","chars":"Zach, JH","title":"THE LINE","actLabel":"Act Two"}','2026-03-08T07:06:28.260Z');
INSERT INTO grails_beat_index VALUES(17,22,unistr('Beat 22: INTERNET OFFICIAL\u000aSeq: SEQUENCE 5 — New Connection Fails\u000aAct: Act Two\u000aLocation: INT. TOGG STUDIOS (LIVESTREAM) / INT. ZACH''S SHOP\u000aCharacters: Togg, Elizabeth, Zach (watching alone)\u000aPlot Goal: Remove Zach''s reason for protecting Elizabeth\u000aCharacter Goal: Zach wants to believe she''s being used; he has to watch her choose it\u000aThe Action: Togg and Elizabeth go internet official — a PR move timed perfectly to deflect the growing authenticity questions around his collection. On camera. Designed. She''s smiling. Zach watches from his shop. He has been replaced by the one person he hates most in the world.\u000aThe Opposition: The truth of what he''s watching — she didn''t fall for the lifestyle, she chose it\u000aStakes: EVERYTHING BLOWS UP. Zach picks up his phone. He calls JH. He''s back in.'),'{"seq":"SEQUENCE 5 — New Connection Fails","chars":"Togg, Elizabeth, Zach (watching alone)","title":"INTERNET OFFICIAL","actLabel":"Act Two"}','2026-03-08T07:06:28.618Z');
INSERT INTO grails_beat_index VALUES(18,23,unistr('Beat 23: THE TAIL\u000aSeq: SEQUENCE 5 — New Connection Fails\u000aAct: Act Two\u000aLocation: EXT. LOS ANGELES — DAY\u000aCharacters: Zach, police (unseen)\u000aPlot Goal: Introduce the police threat — the noose tightening\u000aCharacter Goal: Zach has no idea he''s being followed\u000aThe Action: Zach goes about his business — suppliers, the shop, a meeting with JH. He doesn''t notice the car. The audience does.\u000aThe Opposition: The investigation closing in; Zach''s obliviousness\u000aStakes: Zach is now being watched. He doesn''t know it.'),'{"seq":"SEQUENCE 5 — New Connection Fails","chars":"Zach, police (unseen)","title":"THE TAIL","actLabel":"Act Two"}','2026-03-08T07:06:28.978Z');
INSERT INTO grails_beat_index VALUES(19,26,unistr('Beat 26: THE LIQUIDATION — HERO PROCEEDS UNCERTAINLY\u000aSeq: SEQUENCE 6 — Sacrifice for True Change\u000aAct: Act Two\u000aLocation: INT. ZACH''S SHOP — DAY\u000aCharacters: Zach, [financial trigger TBD]\u000aPlot Goal: Take everything from Zach — strip him to nothing; he moves forward anyway\u000aCharacter Goal: Zach wants to hold on; there is nothing left to hold\u000aThe Action: Financial trigger forces Zach to close his father''s shop. The family heirloom collectibles — everything his father built — go to liquidation. He boxes them himself. The loupe around his neck. The shop dark for the last time.\u000aThe Opposition: The math. The world. The fact that he always knew this was coming.\u000aStakes: Zach has nothing left. He''s all in — not because he chose it but because there''s nowhere else to go.'),'{"seq":"SEQUENCE 6 — Sacrifice for True Change","chars":"Zach, [financial trigger TBD]","title":"THE LIQUIDATION — HERO PROCEEDS UNCERTAINLY","actLabel":"Act Two"}','2026-03-08T07:06:29.338Z');
INSERT INTO grails_beat_index VALUES(20,30,unistr('Beat 30: THE POSITIONS — PLOT POINT II\u000aSeq: SEQUENCE 6 — Sacrifice for True Change\u000aAct: Act Two\u000aLocation: INT. DEJA''S APARTMENT — NIGHT\u000aCharacters: JH, Deja, Hye-Jin, Zach\u000aPlot Goal: Final preparations — everyone in position; the true Plot Point II that locks the act\u000aCharacter Goal: Each crew member wants the job done; each carries something personal into it\u000aThe Action: The crew assembles. Market positions confirmed — $GOAT shorted, prediction market plays set. Zach delivers the box. He looks at it one last time.\u000aThe Opposition: The timing. The police. JH''s personal liability (the revenge vs. the discipline).\u000aStakes: Everything is set. The livestream is tomorrow.'),'{"seq":"SEQUENCE 6 — Sacrifice for True Change","chars":"JH, Deja, Hye-Jin, Zach","title":"THE POSITIONS — PLOT POINT II","actLabel":"Act Two"}','2026-03-08T07:06:29.697Z');
INSERT INTO grails_beat_index VALUES(21,31,unistr('Beat 31: THE LIVESTREAM — ENEMY GETS EGO DRUNK\u000aSeq: SEQUENCE 7 — Triumph via Connection\u000aAct: Act Three\u000aLocation: INT. TOGG EVENT SPACE — NIGHT (LIVESTREAM)\u000aCharacters: Togg, Elizabeth, Hye-Jin, Deja, Zach (offscreen), JH (offscreen)\u000aPlot Goal: The heist executes; the enemy, drunk on ego, gives the hero the space he needs\u000aCharacter Goal: Every character wants something different from this moment\u000aThe Action: The livestream. Togg in his Panopticon. Hye-Jin and Deja in position — invisible, watching. Elizabeth at the authentication station. The box arrives.\u000aThe Opposition: Everything that can go wrong\u000aStakes: The authentication begins. Togg is exposed, but doesn''t know it yet.'),'{"seq":"SEQUENCE 7 — Triumph via Connection","chars":"Togg, Elizabeth, Hye-Jin, Deja, Zach (offscreen), JH (offscreen)","title":"THE LIVESTREAM — ENEMY GETS EGO DRUNK","actLabel":"Act Three"}','2026-03-08T07:06:30.042Z');
INSERT INTO grails_beat_index VALUES(22,32,unistr('Beat 32: THE AUTHENTICATION — HERO CONFRONTS ENEMY FACE TO FACE\u000aSeq: SEQUENCE 7 — Triumph via Connection\u000aAct: Act Three\u000aLocation: INT. TOGG EVENT SPACE — NIGHT (LIVESTREAM)\u000aCharacters: Elizabeth, Togg, crowd\u000aPlot Goal: Elizabeth''s AI passes the forgery; the hero''s work confronts the enemy directly\u000aCharacter Goal: Elizabeth wants to do her job perfectly; Togg wants the spectacle\u000aThe Action: Elizabeth runs the box through her AI. The system processes. The crowd watches. The verdict: authentic.\u000aThe Opposition: Elizabeth''s instincts — something feels off\u000aStakes: The box is authenticated. $GOAT surges. Prediction market locks in.'),'{"seq":"SEQUENCE 7 — Triumph via Connection","chars":"Elizabeth, Togg, crowd","title":"THE AUTHENTICATION — HERO CONFRONTS ENEMY FACE TO FACE","actLabel":"Act Three"}','2026-03-08T07:06:30.399Z');
INSERT INTO grails_beat_index VALUES(23,33,unistr('Beat 33: THE JORDAN DROPS — ECHO OF THE MODIFIER\u000aSeq: SEQUENCE 7 — Triumph via Connection\u000aAct: Act Three\u000aLocation: INT. TOGG EVENT SPACE — NIGHT (LIVESTREAM)\u000aCharacters: Togg, Elizabeth, crowd, Hye-Jin, Deja\u000aPlot Goal: Togg opens the box — the Jordan surfaces; the echo of Zach''s craft resonates\u000aCharacter Goal: Togg wants the moment; the crew wants the market to peak\u000aThe Action: Togg opens the pack. Live. The Jordan rookie card surfaces. The crowd loses its mind. $GOAT goes stratospheric. The prediction market resolves. The crew''s positions are printing.\u000aThe Opposition: None — this is the false peak; the modifier''s signal is hidden inside it\u000aStakes: The crew has won — financially. Now Elizabeth.'),'{"seq":"SEQUENCE 7 — Triumph via Connection","chars":"Togg, Elizabeth, crowd, Hye-Jin, Deja","title":"THE JORDAN DROPS — ECHO OF THE MODIFIER","actLabel":"Act Three"}','2026-03-08T07:06:30.750Z');
INSERT INTO grails_beat_index VALUES(24,34,unistr('Beat 34: THE UNDOTTED I — THE STILLED WORLD COMES TO HIS AID\u000aSeq: SEQUENCE 7 — Triumph via Connection\u000aAct: Act Three\u000aLocation: INT. TOGG EVENT SPACE — NIGHT (LIVESTREAM)\u000aCharacters: Elizabeth, Togg, crowd\u000aPlot Goal: Elizabeth sees the signal — the world confirms the hero has learned the only lesson\u000aCharacter Goal: Elizabeth wants to be wrong; she knows she''s not\u000aThe Action: Elizabeth examines the Jordan. Her AI passed it. But she sees something — the undotted i on the back of the card. The private signal. The thing only she and Zach would know. Her face doesn''t change. She says nothing.\u000aThe Opposition: The livestream. The crowd. Togg''s arm around her. Millions watching.\u000aStakes: Elizabeth knows. She can''t prove it. The question of what she does with that knowledge is the film''s final movement.'),'{"seq":"SEQUENCE 7 — Triumph via Connection","chars":"Elizabeth, Togg, crowd","title":"THE UNDOTTED I — THE STILLED WORLD COMES TO HIS AID","actLabel":"Act Three"}','2026-03-08T07:06:31.098Z');
INSERT INTO grails_beat_index VALUES(25,35,unistr('Beat 35: THE CRASH — THE CLIMAX\u000aSeq: SEQUENCE 7 — Triumph via Connection\u000aAct: Act Three\u000aLocation: INT. TOGG EVENT SPACE / EXT. INTERNET — NIGHT\u000aCharacters: Togg, Elizabeth, crowd, Hye-Jin, Deja\u000aPlot Goal: The fraud leaks — the financial collapse executes; the enemy dies at his moment of greatest ego\u000aCharacter Goal: The crew wants clean exit; Togg wants to stop the bleeding\u000aThe Action: Word spreads — the collection is under question. $GOAT craters. The prediction market flips 1 to 99 in real time. Togg''s empire collapses on livestream, in front of everyone who was watching him win.\u000aThe Opposition: Togg''s PR machine — scrambling, too late\u000aStakes: The crew has won. The question is what comes after.'),'{"seq":"SEQUENCE 7 — Triumph via Connection","chars":"Togg, Elizabeth, crowd, Hye-Jin, Deja","title":"THE CRASH — THE CLIMAX","actLabel":"Act Three"}','2026-03-08T07:06:31.453Z');
INSERT INTO grails_beat_index VALUES(26,36,unistr('Beat 36: GONE LEGIT — THE REWARD\u000aSeq: SEQUENCE 8 — Denouement\u000aAct: Act Three\u000aLocation: INT. NEW OFFICE / EXT. LOS ANGELES — DAY\u000aCharacters: Zach, JH, Deja, Hye-Jin\u000aPlot Goal: Close the loop — the crew has become brokers for elite collectibles; hero gets the hard-earned reward\u000aCharacter Goal: Each character has what they wanted; the world is different now\u000aThe Action: The crew — gone legit. Brokers for the world''s most elite collectibles. Zach''s expertise is finally valued at its real price. Deja runs the operation. Hye-Jin reads the clients. JH is the network.\u000a\u000aZach buys back his father''s collection at auction — every piece, with his own money. He brings them to the new space. Same loupe around his neck. Same reverence. Everything different.\u000aThe Opposition: None — this is the reward\u000aStakes: Trading Places ending. The good criminals beat the bad establishment. The loop is closed.'),'{"seq":"SEQUENCE 8 — Denouement","chars":"Zach, JH, Deja, Hye-Jin","title":"GONE LEGIT — THE REWARD","actLabel":"Act Three"}','2026-03-08T07:06:31.785Z');
INSERT INTO grails_beat_index VALUES(27,37,unistr('Beat 37: THE LOUPE\u000aSeq: SEQUENCE 8 — Denouement\u000aAct: Act Three\u000aLocation: TBD — day or night\u000aCharacters: Zach, Elizabeth\u000aPlot Goal: The final question between them — open, not resolved; the modifier''s final move\u000aCharacter Goal: Both want to be known; neither knows how to say it\u000aThe Action: Elizabeth and Zach. She has the loupe in her hand — out of the pocket. She doesn''t accuse him. She doesn''t have to. He doesn''t confirm it. He doesn''t have to. The question hangs.\u000aThe Opposition: Everything they are to each other\u000aStakes: Open question. Not resolved. The audience carries it out of the theater.'),'{"seq":"SEQUENCE 8 — Denouement","chars":"Zach, Elizabeth","title":"THE LOUPE","actLabel":"Act Three"}','2026-03-08T07:06:32.127Z');
